Hello everyone, I'm struggling with kernel density plots.
I' ve already achieved this with photographs, and due to problems with the videos, I decided to add them manually in the excel table generated by R with the metadata of the pictures that do work.
Using the exactly same format and according to the present values, I calculated the "deltatime" for each video record, and then this error appeared:

> activityDensity(recordTable = SEMINARIO_MANUAL, species = geoffroy, xlab = "Hora", ylab = "Densidad") Warning message: GEOFFROY: Error in densityPlot(subset_species$Time.rad, main = paste("Activity of", :  Bandwidth estimation failed. - SKIPPED

The excel column format used:
Station Species DateTimeOriginal Date Time delta.time.secs delta.time.mins delta.time.hours delta.time.days Directory FileName n_images

Is there any way to make it work, also making it possible to consider only the independent records for the graphs from this modified table?

I really would appreciate some help please! Good night!

